    "blocks_daydAE": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "ai_gen_block_87b20c9_a3xwjd": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_87b20c9",
          "settings": {
            "container_width": 1200,
            "left_column_width": 40,
            "right_column_width": 60,
            "column_gap": 80,
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "heading": "The practical bit: what this means when you are buying",
            "heading_font": "serif",
            "heading_size": 54,
            "mobile_heading_size": 38,
            "heading_color": "#000000",
            "heading_indent": 15,
            "mobile_heading_indent": 15,
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/The_practical_bit_what_this_means_when_you_are_buying_1_99aa6628-5aca-4ffa-8b71-3c2a32e68ade.png",
            "image_max_width": 600,
            "heading_image_gap": 4,
            "mobile_heading_image_gap": 25,
            "body_text": "<p>If your current fragrance keeps disappearing before the afternoon, there is a very good chance you are wearing an EDT and your skin runs dry. The fix is either to move to an EDP of the same fragrance, to moisturise before you spray, or both. Twelve seconds of unscented moisturiser before application makes a significant difference to how long any concentration holds.</p><p>If you find your fragrance feels a bit much in warm weather or close spaces (you know when you’re in an elevator in those 3 days of British summer), you are probably wearing an EDP or Parfum when an EDT would suit the moment better. Concentration is not about quality. It is about fit.</p>",
            "body_font": "system_ui_n4",
            "body_size": 24,
            "mobile_body_size": 16,
            "body_color": "#111111",
            "paragraph_spacing": 30,
            "mobile_paragraph_spacing": 15,
            "text_vertical_offset": 100,
            "background_color": "#f5f3ee",
            "padding_top": 40,
            "padding_bottom": 40,
            "horizontal_padding": 40,
            "mobile_padding_top": 60,
            "mobile_padding_bottom": 60,
            "mobile_horizontal_padding": 20,
            "mobile_gap": 40
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "ai_gen_block_87b20c9_a3xwjd"
      ],
      "name": "Editorial section",
      "settings": {}
    },
    "blocks_UXR9hM": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "ai_gen_block_3a2b0a1_D4QJ4w": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_3a2b0a1",
          "settings": {
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "max_width": 1200,
            "section_padding": 20,
            "background_color": "#f9f6f1",
            "heading": "<p>The verdict</p>",
            "heading_size": 50,
            "heading_color": "#121212",
            "heading_spacing": 10,
            "box_color": "#8b1d22",
            "box_radius": 25,
            "box_padding": 40,
            "box_spacing": 10,
            "box_paragraph_1": "<p>If you have been spending £150 or more on a bottle of fragrance and wearing it sparingly because it feels too precious for an ordinary day, a quality inspired alternative is worth trying properly. Not as a consolation prize. As a genuine option.</p><p>The question is not whether it smells exactly the same. It is whether it smells good enough to wear every day, with confidence, at a price that means you actually will. For the fragrances in the Scentspired range, the answer is yes. Browse the full collection for perfume online shopping any time, with every fragrance listed by notes and inspiration so you know exactly what you are getting before you spend a penny.</p>",
            "box_paragraph_2": "",
            "box_paragraph_3": "",
            "box_text_color": "#ffffff",
            "box_text_size": 24,
            "box_text_line_height": 1.6,
            "paragraph_spacing": 25,
